### OrderFlow — request notebook (VS Code "REST Client" / JetBrains HTTP client)
### Log in first; the cookie is kept by the client for the following requests.

@base = http://localhost:5000

### Log in as a customer
POST {{base}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "bob", "password": "bob" }

### Log in as the manager
POST {{base}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "manager", "password": "manager" }

### Catalogue (no login needed)
GET {{base}}/api/products

### Catalogue search
GET {{base}}/api/products?q=desk

### My orders (customers see their own; the manager sees everyone's)
GET {{base}}/api/orders?page=1&pageSize=10

### Search orders
GET {{base}}/api/orders?q=OF-2026

### One order
GET {{base}}/api/orders/2

### A demo order and its invoice (alice's, paid)
GET {{base}}/api/orders/17

###
GET {{base}}/api/orders/17/invoice

### Create a draft order (a customer orders for themselves; a manager passes customerId)
POST {{base}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "promoCode": null, "lines": [ { "productId": 5, "quantity": 2 }, { "productId": 8, "quantity": 1 } ] }

### Add a line to a draft order
POST {{base}}/api/orders/17/lines
Content-Type: application/json

{ "productId": 3, "quantity": 4 }

### Place / pay / ship a draft order
POST {{base}}/api/orders/17/place

###
POST {{base}}/api/orders/17/pay

###
POST {{base}}/api/orders/17/ship

### Invoice of a paid order
GET {{base}}/api/orders/2/invoice

### Customers (manager)
GET {{base}}/api/customers

### Change a customer's address
PUT {{base}}/api/customers/2/address
Content-Type: application/json

{ "address": "Svobody Ave 10", "city": "Lviv", "country": "Ukraine" }

### --- Release 1.1: diagnostics ---

### Restore the demo data (manager); also clears the outbox and the request log
POST {{base}}/api/test/reset

### E-mails sent since start-up or the last reset, newest first
GET {{base}}/api/outbox

### Request log, newest first (manager)
GET {{base}}/api/log

### Log out
POST {{base}}/api/auth/logout
